messages.body:
Hi {{contact.first_name}},

Thanks for getting in touch with {{location.name}}. Your details are with us and somebody will call you back on the number you left.

If it is easier, you can take a time straight off the calendar here: {{custom_values.booking_link}}

Three things help us arrive with the right parts: what the equipment is doing, roughly how old it is, and whether you are without heating or cooling right now. Reply with whatever you know.

{{location.name}}
{{location.phone}}

Hi {{contact.first_name}},

Thanks for writing to {{location.name}}. The office is closed at the moment and opens again at {{custom_values.opening_time}} on the next working day. Your message is already in the queue for the morning, so there is nothing you need to send twice.

If you would rather not wait, you can hold a time yourself here: {{custom_values.booking_link}}

If you have no heat or no cooling and it will not keep until morning, reply with the word urgent and your address, and the on-call technician is paged instead.

{{location.name}}
